INEOS holds refresher training on the Plan annually.

To ensure proper functioning, INEOS emergency response equipment is regularly inspected and serviced.  In addition, the ER Plan will be promptly updated when and as necessary to reflect any changes taking place within the processes that would require a modified emergency response.

INEOS coordinates its emergency response plan and activities with the Iberville Parish Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC).  The INEOS emergency response team also works closely with Dow's LAO Emergency, Safety and Security (ES&S) team, and personnel from the two companies are qualified to provide mutual emergency assistance when necessary.  Lines of communication have been clearly established between the two companies with respect to sharing emergency and chemical hazard information.

6.	Planned Changes to Improve Safety

There are no planned changes to improve safety at this time as a result of the plant implementing the accidental release prevention program.
